ike that mean that is meaningless at  the moment um and i think again there's  there's a big question mark as to  um if and when we will we will see the  fda come out with a real definition that  can give consumers a little more  confidence in that claim  last thing i want to ask about and i  know we're now getting like a couple  levels removed from from where we  started  homeopathic products  herbal products some supplements etc  where they say  statements have not been evaluated by  the fda  etc we've all seen that type of thing  um what are the concerns and sort of  what is in that general space that  consumers should be aware of when  looking at those products  yeah now you're a couple steps from my  bellywick um  they're they're even you know i've  already said already that there's a lot  of claims on foods that um either fda  hasn't yet defined like natural they  don't really have a great definition um  or where there is a very clear  definition but they just don't have the  resources to enforce  once you get into supplements um you  know herbal things etc  it's even more so that way i mean a lot  of people in the food space will call  that really the wild west in terms of  the  um  in terms of the the level of both laws  and enforcement  um so i think it's it's a really  difficult area i think there's a lot of  folks calling for more regulation there  and  you know making sure both that  there's really two concerns one is when  you buy a supplement is what's in there  actually what it says it is right and  the second is are the claims about what  it can do for your health validated in  any way and i think on both ends of that  it's a really big question mark and it's  hard for the companies that are you know  trying to do it well and and trying to  do a good job because i think they will  probably like more enforcement so that  they you know they're they're that  people will have more trust in that  space yeah with without a doubt um emily  broadley is a clinical professor of law  and faculty director for harvard law  school's food law and policy clinic  really appreciate your time today  great talking to you thanks
 

